(SMARTGYM USER MANUAL) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This manual explains how to use the SmartGym Adaptive Training System as an evaluator,) Tj
T*
(athlete, or demo user.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Turning On the Device) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Connect power to the ESP32-S3 display.) Tj
T*
(2. Wait for the main screen to appear.) Tj
T*
(3. Allow the device to connect to Wi-Fi, Firebase, RFID, and time services.) Tj
T*
(4. Do not start a workout until the device reaches the ready state.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. RFID Login) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Place the RFID card near the reader.) Tj
T*
(2. The screen shows a loading popup.) Tj
T*
(3. Keep waiting until the popup closes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The popup remains visible while the device loads:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- User profile.) Tj
T*
(- User calibration for the active machine.) Tj
T*
(- Recommendation for the active user and machine.) Tj
T*
(- Calibrated ROM mapping.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The user should not press START or CALIBRATE while the loading popup is active.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Main Screen) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The main screen shows the current session state, live motion graph, pin load,) Tj
T*
(recommendation, reps, sets, and action buttons.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Important terms:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Pin load: the physical weight pin position on the machine.) Tj
T*
(- Recommended load: the load suggested by SmartGym for the active user.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The pin load belongs to the machine, not the user. It does not automatically change) Tj
T*
(when a different user scans an RFID card. The recommendation is user-specific advice.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Pin Load vs Recommended Load) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The system never physically moves the weight pin. If the screen recommends 25.0 kg but) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
