BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 760 Td
14 TL
(the machine pin is at 20.0 kg, the device shows both values separately:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Pin load: 20.0 kg) Tj
T*
(- Recommended: 25.0 kg) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If the user wants to follow the recommendation, they must physically move the pin and) Tj
T*
(then update the displayed pin load with the touchscreen buttons.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Changing Pin Load) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use the four weight buttons:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `-5`) Tj
T*
(- `-2.5`) Tj
T*
(- `+2.5`) Tj
T*
(- `+5`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(These buttons update the displayed machine pin load. They do not change the) Tj
T*
(recommendation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Pin load can be changed before training or during training. If it changes during) Tj
T*
(training, later reps are recorded with the new load.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Starting a Workout) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Scan RFID and wait for loading to finish.) Tj
T*
(2. Check the pin load.) Tj
T*
(3. Physically set the machine pin if needed.) Tj
T*
(4. Adjust the on-screen pin load to match the physical pin.) Tj
T*
(5. Press START.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The session starts using the displayed pin load exactly as shown.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Following the Graph) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The graph shows motion through the exercise range. The firmware uses ROM, or range of) Tj
T*
(motion, to detect repetitions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The user-facing cues focus on timing, for example:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Rise time.) Tj
T*
(- Lower time.) Tj
T*
(- Top hold.) Tj
T*
(- Bottom hold.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
