(The system avoids showing raw technical values such as `%ROM/s` in the main user) Tj
T*
(interface.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8. Reps and Sets) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The firmware detects reps from the ROM signal. A rep must move through enough range) Tj
T*
(and pass the internal validation rules.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The screen shows:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Current reps in the set.) Tj
T*
(- Current set.) Tj
T*
(- Training state.) Tj
T*
(- Timer or progress where available.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If a rep is not counted, possible causes include short range of motion, noisy) Tj
T*
(movement, or not reaching the top/bottom thresholds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(9. Rest and Finishing) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(When the target reps for a set are completed, the system marks the set complete.) Tj
T*
(Depending on the target set count, the session may auto-finish or continue to the next) Tj
T*
(set.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The user can also finish manually by pressing FINISH.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10. Summary Screen and Sync) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(After finishing, the summary screen appears. It may show:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Session complete.) Tj
T*
(- Pin load used.) Tj
T*
(- New recommendation.) Tj
T*
(- Save/upload status.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Typical save states:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Saving session...) Tj
T*
(- Uploading core...) Tj
T*
(- Uploading details...) Tj
T*
(- Uploading reps...) Tj
T*
(- Session saved.) Tj
T*
(- Saving in background.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If sync is still running, the device can continue saving in the background. Do not) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
