(power off immediately after a workout if the screen still indicates saving.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11. Calibration) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Calibration should be used when:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- A new user uses the machine.) Tj
T*
(- ROM looks incorrect.) Tj
T*
(- Recommendations are missing.) Tj
T*
(- The system says to calibrate first.) Tj
T*
(- The exercise setup has changed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Calibration Steps) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Press CALIBRATE.) Tj
T*
(2. Read the step title and instruction.) Tj
T*
(3. Move the physical pin to the suggested load if appropriate.) Tj
T*
(4. Use the calibration screen's four pin-load buttons if the displayed pin does not match) Tj
T*
(   the physical pin.) Tj
T*
(5. Tap LOAD SET.) Tj
T*
(6. Perform 3 to 5 smooth reps.) Tj
T*
(7. Follow any next-load instruction.) Tj
T*
(8. Save the result when complete.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The calibration screen shows:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Pin load.) Tj
T*
(- Suggested load.) Tj
T*
(- Weight adjustment buttons.) Tj
T*
(- Rep feedback.) Tj
T*
(- Save/cancel actions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If the pin load differs from the suggested load, the user may still continue, but the) Tj
T*
(device logs that the user chose a different physical pin.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12. Recommendations) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Recommendations are generated from calibration and session history. They are advice) Tj
T*
(only. The system does not automatically change the physical pin load.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Recommendation sources may include:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Calibration.) Tj
T*
(- Last session.) Tj
T*
(- Machine default.) Tj
T*
(- No recommendation.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
